TI  - Development of a Machine Identity Management System for Microservices with a NoSQL Backend in Zero Trust Conditions
AU  - Kunniev, H. M.
T2  - Automatic documentation and mathematical linguistics
AB  - The article addresses the challenge of securing service-to-service communication in distributed microservice architectures. Traditional perimeter-based security models are losing relevance in dynamically scalable cloud environments. We propose an architecture for a machine identity management system based on Zero Trust principles. A distinctive feature of the solution is the use of a scalable NoSQL backend for storing access policies and audit logs. The economic risks of implementation are analyzed, and the effectiveness of the proposed approach is evaluated in terms of reducing the probability of information security incidents. The results demonstrate the feasibility of achieving a balance between system security and performance.
